<%# Flash toasts for public, customer-facing pages, rendered once from the
    shared application layout so every public page can show notices. Owner
    pages have their own equivalent at owner/shared/_flash, rendered from the
    separate owner layout; both float the same `.toast-stack` and render the
    same `shared/_flash_band`.

    The stack is fixed to the bottom-right corner of the viewport and is only
    in the document when there is something to say — a flash costs this page no
    space and no reflow either way. Width and gutters belong to `.toast-stack`
    now; there is no per-page narrowing hook any more, because a floating band
    is not sitting above a form column to begin with.

    data-turbo-temporary: Turbo caches the page as it leaves it and paints that
    snapshot instantly on back/forward before the fresh fetch arrives. A flash
    baked into the snapshot is a message the reader has already dealt with —
    and it does not come back quietly, it slides in and arms a fresh six-second
    timer, so it reads as something new having just happened. The attribute
    tells Turbo to drop the element before caching. %>
<% if notice || alert %>
  <div class="toast-stack" data-turbo-temporary>
    <% if notice %>
      <%= render "shared/flash_band",
                 variant: "alert-success",
                 icon_name: "check-circle",
                 label: t("shared.flash_notice"),
                 message: notice %>
    <% end %>
    <% if alert %>
      <%= render "shared/flash_band",
                 variant: "alert-error",
                 icon_name: "warning",
                 label: t("shared.flash_error"),
                 message: alert %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
